                "row_limit": null,
                "filters_supported": true,
                "realtime": false
            },
            "extraction_path": "custom_pull",
            "verification_expected_rows_per_day": null,
            "_api_notes": "VERIFIE le 2026-07-21 (doc officielle) : endpoint GET https://automate.adjust.com/reports-service/report (Report Service API, JSON). Params: dimensions= et metrics= (CSV), date_period=YYYY-MM-DD:YYYY-MM-DD, utc_offset, app_token__in (filtre de scope), sandbox. Le grain jour vient de la dimension 'day'. Les valeurs de metriques arrivent en CHAINES dans rows[] (ex: \"64\") et en nombres dans totals{}. Source : https://dev.adjust.com/en/api/rs-api/reports"
        }
    ],
    "canonical_metric_mapping": {
        "cost": "cost",
        "installs": "installs",
        "clicks": "clicks",
        "impressions": "impressions",
        "sessions": "sessions",
        "revenue": "revenue",
        "ad_revenue": "ad_revenue",
        "all_revenue": "all_revenue"
    },
    "canonical_dimension_mapping": {
        "day": "date",
        "app_token": "app_token",
        "app": "app",
        "network": "network",
        "campaign_id_network": "campaign_id",
        "campaign_network": "campaign_name",
        "currency_code": "cost_source_currency"
    },
    "error_map": {
        "401": "auth_expired",
        "403": "permission_denied",
        "400": "invalid_request",
        "503": "provider_transient",
        "504": "provider_transient",
        "_error_map_note": "Adjust Report Service API documents HTTP statuses only (200/204/400/401/403/429/503/504 -- https://dev.adjust.com/en/api/rs-api/reports Response codes) and publishes NO finite enumeration of provider sub-codes in error bodies. This map is therefore keyed on HTTP status alone (no ':provider_code' refinement); the pure-HTTP classification in core.pull_errors._base_class_for_status already lands 401->auth_expired, 403->permission_denied, 400->invalid_request, 5xx->provider_transient (503/504 included). 429 raises core.quota.RateLimitError (breaker path). A later story can add '<status>:<code>' keys if Adjust introduces stable sub-codes."
    },
    "account_topology": {
        "_comment": "Playbook section 5: Adjust topology is a single flat level -- the API token's reachable APPS. The reporting entity (selection_level) is the APP (app_token); a selected app narrows the pull via the app_token__in filter and every row carries app_token as a dimension. discover_accounts calls the official Filters Data endpoint (GET https://automate.adjust.com/reports-service/filters_data?required_filters=apps) which lists the apps the token can reach ({id, name}). No *_ACCOUNT_ID env var exists for this module (the 25.5+ standard): without a selected app the pull stays scoped to the token's own account (all its apps), never to an ambient environment value.",
        "levels": [
            {
                "id": "app",
                "label": "App"
            }
        ],
        "selection_level": "app",
        "discovery": {
            "callable": "discover_accounts"
        }
    },
    "quota": {
        "window_seconds": 60,
        "budget_points": 600,
        "read_cost": 1,
        "write_cost": 1,
        "_rate_limit_note": "VERIFIE le 2026-07-21 : le Report Service API applique 50 requetes/seconde par IP source (burst 100) -- https://dev.adjust.com/en/api/rs-api/rate-limits. Le profil retenu (600 points / 60s, soit 10 req/s en moyenne) est volontairement conservateur car la limite est PAR IP (partagee entre connexions derriere le meme NAT). Backstop: handler 429 -> RateLimitError."
    },
    "_ad4_notes": {
        "revenue": "REGLE AD-4 (miroir stripe/shopify 15.7) : 'revenue' Adjust = revenu in-app mesure par le SDK Adjust (meme grandeur canonique que le revenue commerce). Il n'est JAMAIS somme dans un total croise avec le revenue Shopify/Stripe : la regle declarative metric_source_priority.csv porte revenue -> shopify 1, stripe 2, adjust 3 ; la vue cross_source_revenue choisit UNE source gagnante par (projet, jour). Les lignes par source restent interrogeables independamment (fact_daily_kpi keye sur connector).",
        "sessions": "REGLE AD-4 : 'sessions' Adjust (sessions app mesurees SDK) et 'sessions' GA4 (sessions web/app GA) mesurent des proprietes DIFFERENTES. fact_daily_kpi les separe par connector ; elles ne sont jamais sommees en un total croise (comparaison canal par canal uniquement, meme discipline que klaviyo attributed_*)."
    },
    "widget_ref": "ui://core/daily-report",
